<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">sprung off in the spring time</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;A thick silence follows as Glimmer struggles to take in this information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The savior of the universe. Fell asleep standing. Then tumbled through a building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Glimmer was &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; trained for this.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra begins uncontrollably laughing. Just joyful full-body squeaky laughs that she doesn't even attempt to hide. It seems to actually wake Adora out of her stupor a bit, blushing and staring fondly at Catra as if no one else can see her doing so.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Slowly, the queen looks to Adora and then to Catra. They immediately straighten right up, used to being under the scrutiny of a commanding officer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œBoth of you. Throne room. In two hours.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Glimmer's so so tired of Catra and Adora. The infuriating (yet helpful) decrees, the tireless overworking, the general uselessness and hopeless pining that seems to have followed them since the Heart of Etheria a couple months ago, the &lt;em&gt;destroying her castle&lt;/em&gt;. With Netossa and Spinnerella, she decides to solve all this by sending them off on a secret mission. They just have to infiltrate a cult of Plumerian citizens and find out some info. And if they stumble into a journey of discoveries along the way, well, thatâ€™s their own fucking problem.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>petty_labelle</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
